abstract: >
  AutoApply (AA) is an open-source automated job application platform that
  simultaneously serves as a scientific research instrument for studying
  hiring system dysfunction. AA operates from the candidate's perspective
  across hundreds of Applicant Tracking System (ATS) platforms, detecting
  ghost job postings, salary transparency law violations, discriminatory
  language patterns, qualification inflation, and regulatory non-compliance.
  The platform implements a hexagonal (Ports and Adapters) architecture with
  a mathematical DOM perception subsystem, enabling reproducible, seeded
  execution for research-grade data collection. AA produces publishable
  datasets on hiring market dysfunction at scales previously impossible
  through manual academic audit studies.
